<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal retail sales rose 2.6 pct yr/yr in Feb.</title>
<headline>Portugal retail sales rose 2.6 pct yr/yr in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's retail sales index rose 2.6 percent year-on-year in February but was down 5.5 percent on the previous month, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>INE gave the following figures for retail sales:</p>
<p>				  Feb 97 (a)   Jan 97 (b)    Feb 96 (b)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)	   135.0	   142.8	  131.5</p>
<p>    Food and drink		152.0	   160.2	  158.7</p>
<p>    Chemical/pharmaceutical   182.7	   193.9	  159.8</p>
<p>    Clothing/footwear/textile 181.3	   228.4	  185.7</p>
<p>    Furniture		     106.0	   116.4	   97.1</p>
<p>    Construction materials    124.6	   112.3	  108.1</p>
<p>    Vehicles			111.5	   113.4	  101.3</p>
<p>    Fuel			    142.4	   150.4	  141.0</p>
<p>    Warehouse/market sales    107.7	   105.9	  106.9</p>
<p>a) previsional figures b) revised -- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
